From 1cd57d2b8c49dff048c21cdbafdb54439a7f07e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andris Reinman <andris@reinman.eu>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:21:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(addressparser): honour quoted strings and comments inside
 an angle-addr and a group

The tokenizer tracks a single open operator, so once '<' or ':' was open
it only looked for the '>' or ';' that closes it and was blind to the
quoted strings, comments and domain literals in between.

A '>' inside a quoted local part therefore ended the angle-addr and the
domain was read off the text in front of it: '<"a@evil.com>"@good.com>'
put an address at evil.com into the envelope where RFC 5322 reads the
mailbox "a@evil.com>"@good.com. The unbracketed spelling was already
read correctly. A ';' inside a quoted display name or a comment ended a
group and the rest was parsed again with the quoting flipped, so
'G: (a; <evil@evil.com>) <v@victim.com>;' delivered to evil@evil.com
only, where every conformant reading names v@victim.com only.

The tokenizer now follows quoted strings and comments, with their
backslash escapes, inside both, and domain literals inside an angle-addr,
and reads the closer only outside them. The characters are still
collected as before, the angle-addr and the group content are read again
later, so only the point where they end moves. An unclosed quoted string,
comment or domain literal runs to the end of the value, as an unclosed
quoted string or comment outside the brackets does. A domain literal is
not tracked in a group, where a ';' or ',' inside one still ends it, so
an unclosed '[' can not swallow the recipients after it (#1829).

Differential fuzz over 812k unique inputs against the previous
implementation: 96720 parses change, every one holds a '"', '(' or '['
together with a '<' or ':'. Of the changed parses that Python's email
package reads without defects, the recipient domains now agree with it
in 8707 of 8992 cases, against 328 before.

Fixes GHSA-85x2-q946-cp5h
Fixes GHSA-m943-m63m-w62w

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
